:: Stage 0 Plan [event main_quest] {"position":"3025,125","size":"100,100"}
/* The rules of the house in his words (PLAYER_BACKSTORY.md): liked or useful. He won't ask mom for money again the way he
   did after the cafe dropped him; the next time, the device does the asking (Mom's here to help). */
I shut the door and lean against it for a second. My room is the one place in this house where nobody asks me how the company is doing, which makes it the best place to think. I want results, and wanting them isn't a plan. So, let's start working on one.

Money first, because it always is. The diner is the only thing paying me right now, and it isn't paying much. Between the office and the equipment I'm out $<<=$rent>> every week, a number I'd rather not stare at for too long. That means more shifts, more mopping, and more of my manager's little jokes. If things get really tight, there's $mom.callName, but I already know how asking her goes: a cup of tea, my hand held across the table, a no, and a gentle word about something steadier. I'm not doing that again, not like last time anyway. The next time money comes out of her, it won't be because I sat in the kitchen and asked nicely.

So the plan for this house is simple, and it costs me nothing. In this family you're either liked or you're useful, and for the next few weeks I'm going to be both. I'll be the sweet $mom.playerRelation who dries the dishes and tells her the lasagna is the best she's ever made, and the $sister.playerRelation who laughs at $sister.callName's jokes and lets her win at cards. People who like you say yes a lot more often, and people you're useful to say it even faster. I've watched the two of them live on that my whole life. It's about time I got a turn.

Now for the part I actually care about. $company.prototype.name was built to read rooms. If I'm right, it can do more than read them, and if I'm right about that, I'm holding something nobody else has. Proving it takes hours, though. I can grind away at the office, or, on days when even getting there feels like too much, dig through research on the laptop right here. For now the goal is simple: get the prototype to $company.prototype.maxProgress%. Once it's there, I might risk a first test.

Beyond that, my list is pretty short. Mostly I need to survive the first few weeks back home without losing my mind.

